#
# Conformance case: worlds-C/revision (Stratum-C counterfactuals, #505)
# Deterministic AGM revision under the default profile:
#   - consequent : admit status(server, down) -> alert fires (AC-1) without
#                  leaking into the base store (AC-2, asserted by the test).
#   - determined : an over-determined antecedent {primary, backup} arbitrated by
#                  gmeow:overrides -> the more-entrenched value wins (AC-3, one world).
#   - tie        : an over-determined antecedent {blue, green} with no entrenchment
#                  edge -> a genuine tie -> status "unknown" (AC-3, no branch).
#
# The base world's facts (and the gmeow:overrides entrenchment edge) live in
# input.nq; the revision rules + counterfactual queries live in queries/*.logic.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/worlds-c/revision/> .

# Schema: sort used by the projection back-ends.
ex:Thing a logic:Kind .
